## Run it

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

The app opens at `http://localhost:<%= port %>`. URLs and keys are in `.env.local`, which
is not versioned; `.env.sample` lists every variable.

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Dev server |
| `npm run build` | Production build in `dist/` |
| `npm test` | Unit and flow tests (Jest) |
| `npm run verify` | Lint, `link-loom check`, tests and build: run it before every push |
| `npm run version-patch` | Bumps the patch version, tags it and pushes the tag |
| `npm run docker:build` | Builds the image in `docker/Dockerfile` |

## Add to it

Use the CLI so every piece follows the same standard:

```bash
npx link-loom describe --project
npx link-loom add page --domain reports --name Monthly
```

## Docker

`docker/Dockerfile` builds and serves the app with nginx on port 8080 (health check at `/system/health`).
`docker/Dockerfile.runtime` serves a `dist/` you already built: `npm run build && docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.runtime .`
